[00:12.86]<font color="#4096d1">本字幕仅供学习交流，严禁用于商业用途
[00:22.15]<font color="#4096d1">-=破烂熊字幕组=- 翻译:Celeste 校对&时间轴:tpring
[00:36.06]大展宏图
[00:47.36](国防部)
(Ministry of Defence)
[01:14.83]告诉我 将军 热线在哪里?
Tell me, General. Where's the hotline?
[01:17.47]哪一条?      连接俄国的那一条
Which one? The one to Russia.
[01:20.11]"红色热线" 先生
The red hotline, sir.
[01:22.36]在唐宁街
It's in Downing Street.
[01:24.66]紧急情况下我能直接接通苏联主席吗?
I can get through to the Soviet president?
[01:27.38]理论上可以
Theoretically, yes.
[01:28.44]理论上?     我们是这么跟记者说的
Theoretically? That's what we tell journalists.
[01:31.30]确实接通过一次克林姆林宫 那边是个接线员
We once get through to a switchboard operator.
[01:35.87]他不能转过去吗?     不知道 他英语不好
Couldn't he put you through? Never found out.
[01:40.83]这条线多久测试一次?     尽量少测试
How often is it tested? Not too often.
[01:43.47]否则会给另一端带来不必要的恐慌
It creates unnecessary panic at the other end,
[01:46.16]考虑到核武器 还是避免恐慌为好
avoid panic where nuclear weapons are concerned.
[01:50.80]对哦     就是这个
Yes. Now, this is it.
[01:53.75]啊 好
Ah, good.
[01:57.00]这是什么?     扳机 首相
What is it? The trigger, Prime Minister.
[02:00.66]扳机?     核武器扳机 按钮
The trigger? The nuclear trigger, the button.
[02:03.36]这个?     间接地说 是的
This? Indirectly, yes.
[02:06.38]这条电报线直通诺伍德海军基地
This is the telex communication with HMS Northwood.
[02:09.88]您发一个电码 基地通讯员回一个确认码
You send a coded signal and Northwood sends another signal.
[02:15.50]这样他就知道是您了
So he knows it's from you.
[02:17.72]一旦您的指令被确认
When the instruction's been authenticated,
[02:20.39]基地会下令给一艘北极星潜艇 他们就按按钮
Northwood sends a command to a Polaris submarine.
[02:24.58]就这样?     就这样
Just like that? Just like that.
[02:27.16]只要我下命令?     只要您下命令
When I say so? When you say so.
[02:30.30]不会有人跟我争论吗?
Wouldn't anybody argue with me?
[02:33.58]军人的天职是服从 不是提问
Serving officers obey orders without question.
[02:36.47]如果我那时喝醉了呢?
What if I were to get drunk?
[02:39.00]基本上 您别喝醉比较安全
On the whole, it would be safer if you didn't.
[02:42.35]天哪
Blimey!
[02:43.91]这是您的工作 是您要干的 首相
It's your job and you wanted it, Prime Minister.
[02:47.07]假设我昏了头呢?     内阁会发现的
Supposing I were to go off my rocker? The Cabinet might notice.
[02:51.02]我可不指望 说真的 要是我下完令反悔了呢?
I wouldn't count on it. supposing I did and then changed my mind?
[02:56.02]没关系 反正也没人会发现了 不是吗?
That's all right. No one would ever know, would they?
[03:01.63]我们有多少核弹头?
How many bombs are there?
[03:03.11]4艘北极星核潜艇 每艘16颗 各3个弹头
Four Polaris submarines, 16 missiles on each.
[03:07.03]总共呢?      192
But how many actual bombs? 192.
[03:09.91]每一颗至少比广岛的强大5倍
Each one at least five times the power of the Hiroshima bomb.
[03:13.96]我知道您怎么想 "不太多"?
You're thinking, ''Not very many.''
[03:16.50]我不知道 似乎足够了
I don't know. That seems enough.
[03:19.50]比起1200颗瞄准英国的苏联核弹 不算多
Not with 1200 Soviet missiles trained on Britain
[03:23.47]1200?      嗯
1200? Hmm.
[03:25.83]反正大不列颠总是以寡击众
Britain's always fought against the odds
[03:29.10]西班牙无敌舰队 不列颠之战
the Armada, Battle of Britain.
[03:30.55]是的 等我们拥有三叉戟 我们的火力会大大增强
Yes, and we'll have more firepower when we get Trident.
[03:34.78]眼下 谢天谢地还有陆军
Thank goodness for conventional forces!
[03:37.44]陆军最多能拖住俄国人72小时
They would hold the Russians for at most 72 hours.
[03:40.91]就这?      嗯
Is that all? Hmm.
[03:43.07]所以如果有紧急情况发生
So in an emergency
[03:44.41]我就得当机立断作出决定?
I would have to make an instant decision?
[03:46.83]不 您至少有12小时      12小时?
No, you'd probably have 12 hours. 12 hours?
[03:49.91]我们不应该改善这个情况吗?
Shouldn't we do something about this?
[03:52.47]是 但20年以来 政客们总说他们养不起陆军
politicians have said they can't afford the conventional forces.
[03:57.19]陆军太贵了 首相
Conventional forces are very expensive, Prime Minister.
[04:00.35]按一下按钮便宜很多很多
Much cheaper just to press a button.
[04:05.07]那么这次会议您觉得多长时间为好?
So how long should we allow for this meeting?
[04:07.75]72小时...      好的
72 hours... Fine.
[04:11.91]只是新西兰专员而已
It's only the New Zealand High Commissioner.
[04:15.91]72小时是不是太慷慨了点?
Isn't 72 hours a bit generous?
[04:19.19]我只是在想我们能抵挡俄国人多长时间
I was just thinking how long we could hold the Russians.
[04:22.75]如果我们能说服美国人加强他们的陆军...
If we persuaded the Americans to strengthen THEIR forces...
[04:26.95]我觉得这样不会有什么改变
I don't think it'll make much difference.
[04:29.60]在德国的美国军队都磕药
The American troops in Germany are all so drug-ridden,
[04:32.95]他们也不知道自己是哪一边的
they don't know which side they're on anyway.
[04:35.63]上次北约演习的时候
And during the last NATO exercises,
[04:38.23]美国大兵在树林里解散
the U.S. troops dispersed
[04:40.13]然后和女性士兵一起去了树林里野餐
and picnicked in the woods with lady soldiers.
[04:44.23]那么其他的北约军队呢?
What about the other NATO armies?
[04:45.89]他们很好 至少在工作日的时候
They're all right. On weekdays, anyway.
[04:49.30]工作日?
Weekdays?
[04:51.00]对 荷兰 丹麦 比利时军队周末要回家的
The Dutch, Danish and Belgian armies go home for the weekend.
[04:54.67]所以 假定俄国人真要侵略
So if the Russians are to invade
[04:56.92]我们希望他们在周一至周五间侵略?
we'd prefer them to do it between Mondays and Fridays?
[05:00.00]很多人知道这件事吗?
Is this widely known?
[05:02.07]既然我都知道了 俄国人肯定知道
If I know it, I'm sure the Russians do.
[05:04.26]克林姆林宫得到北约消息的速度
The Kremlin usually gets NATO information
[05:06.52]通常比我们唐宁街10号快
before it filters through to Number 10.
[05:10.35]所以我们得依赖三叉戟?      等它送来
So it comes back to Trident? When it comes.
[05:13.75]如果它能用      如果它能...
If it works. If it wor...
[05:17.88]你说什么?      通常新来的武器
What do you mean? Normally, when new weapons are delivered,
[05:21.91]弹头都无法配合火箭架
the warheads don't fit the ends of the rockets.
[05:25.67]北极星就是这样 您知道的
That's what happened to Polaris. You know the sort of thing
[05:28.29]电线不行啦 芯片出错啦
wiring faults, microchip failure.
[05:30.88]有好几年我们都无法正常发射北极星
We couldn't fire Polaris for some years.
[05:34.01]巡航导弹可能也是 还有三叉戟
Cruise is probably the same. Trident might be too.
[05:37.07]这简直不能容忍 我们该把制造商送上法庭
We should take the manufacturers to court.
[05:39.39]我们不能冒被媒体发现的险
We can't risk the publicity
[05:41.57]国家安全 他们是知道的
security and they know it!
[05:43.04]那就不能换一个制造商?
We should change the manufacturers.
[05:44.83]我们总在换的
We do all the time.
[05:47.00]制造商也明白 这就是为什么
The manufacturers know that too. That's why
[05:49.52]一枚鱼雷击中了高尔夫球场
that torpedo landed on Sandwich golf course.
[05:53.55]高尔夫球场?我没在报纸上看到
Sandwich golf course? I didn't read that in the papers.
[05:57.35]当然不会 政府掩盖了消息
Of course not. There was a cover-up.
[06:00.00]只是第二天早上球员们
The members just found a new bunker
[06:01.41]发现第七道旁边多了条沟
on the 7th fairway the next morning.
[06:05.44]所以鱼雷都不能正常工作?
So the torpedoes don't work either?
[06:07.61]不 只是新的 其他的都可以
No, only the new ones. The others are fine.
[06:11.11]二战时候设计出来的的那些
The ones designed during the Second World War.
[06:14.35]40年前的?      对 它们久经测试
Over 40 years ago? They had lots of testing.
[06:17.51]现代武器很难做完这些测试      为什么?
You can't afford that with the modern ones. Why not?
[06:20.88]如果爆发核战 首相 时间不会久到
Well, if there's a nuclear war, it won't last long enough
[06:24.64]能让武器测试完为止
for the weapons to be tested.
[06:26.32]关于国防还有什么事情我得知道的?
Are there other things I don't know about the UK's defence?
[06:29.92]我不知道 首相 我不知道你不知道什么
I don't know, Prime Minister. I don't know what you don't know.
[06:34.55]不过如果您需要不同意见 我知道
The government's chief scientific adviser
[06:36.33]政府首席科学顾问和国防部的看法不太一样
sees the problem differently from the MoD.
[06:40.29]我现在就想见他
I'd like to see him now.
[06:41.91]晚一点邀请他来喝杯酒比较明智
A late drink might be wiser.
[06:43.69]最好别让内阁办公室知道
Better not to let the Cabinet Office know.
[06:46.23]汉弗莱爵士会不高兴的
Sir Humphrey gets upset.
[06:47.33]他不认为那位顾问属于我们的人
He doesn't regard him as one of us.
[06:50.11]我记得他在阿荷姆得过优秀军人勋章
I thought he won the DSO at Arnhem.
[06:52.67]这也不能弥补他古怪的奥地利口音
That doesn't make up for speaking with an Austrian accent.
[06:56.30]他没进过牛津剑桥 甚至伦敦政经学院
He didn't go to Oxford or Cambridge even go to the LSE.
[07:03.60]首相 您相信核武防御吗?
Prime Minister, you believe in the nuclear deterrent?
[07:06.82]哦 是的      为什么?
Oh, yes. Why?
[07:09.00]什么?      为什么?
Pardon? Why?
[07:11.11]因为它能防御
Because it deters.
[07:14.11]谁?      什么?
Whom? Pardon?
[07:16.26]谁?它防御谁?      防御俄国入侵
Whom? Whom does it deter? The Russians from attacking us.
[07:20.79]为什么?      什么?
Why? Pardon?
[07:22.48]什么?
Why?
[07:23.95]他们知道 如果他们侵略我就按按钮
They know if they launched an attack, I'd press the button.
[07:27.39]你会吗?      为什么不会?
You would? Well, wouldn't I?
[07:30.04]你会吗?
Well, would you?
[07:32.19]最后关头 我当然会
At the last resort, yes, I certainly would.
[07:34.88]我想我当然会的 当然
Well, I think I certainly would. Yes.
[07:38.67]几时才算最后关头呢?
And what is the last resort?
[07:41.92]如果俄国侵略西欧的话
If the Russians invaded western Europe.
[07:43.47]可你只有12小时 所以
You only have 12 hours to decide, so you're saying
[07:45.58]你的最后关头就是最初反应?
the last resort is the first response?
[07:48.44]是吗?
Am I?
[07:50.51]不用担心 俄国怎么会想要整个欧洲?
Why should the Russians annex the whole of Europe?
[07:55.55]他们连阿富汗都控制不了
They can't even control Afghanistan.
[07:58.63]不 如果他们尝试侵略 会用"香肠战术"
No, if they try anything, it will be salami tactics.
[08:02.35]香肠?      一片接一片
Salami tactics? Slice by slice.
[08:05.67]每次一小片儿
One small piece at a time.
[08:08.23]当他们侵略西柏林的时候你会按下按钮吗?
So will you press the button if they invade West Berlin?
[08:12.35]看情况      什么情况?
It all depends. On what?
[08:15.35]好吧 第一步
Scenario one.
[08:17.95]西柏林暴动
Riots in West Berlin,
[08:20.60]建筑物在燃烧
buildings in flames.
[08:22.95]东柏林消防队跨界前来救援 你按吗?
East German fire brigade crosses the border. Would you press?
[08:28.88]东柏林警察也过来了 按吗?
The East German police come with them. The button...?
[08:33.00]然后是军队 更多的军队 他们说是来控制骚乱的
Then some troops, more troops just for riot control, they say.
[08:37.47]再然后 俄国军队代替了东德 按吗?
East German troops are replaced by Russian troops. Button?
[08:43.03]俄国军队不肯走了
Then the Russian troops don't go.
[08:45.66]他们受邀留下援助民政部门
They are invited to stay to support civilian administration.
[08:49.63]民政部门关闭了道路和机场
The civilian administration closes roads and Tempelhof Airport.
[08:54.27]现在要按吗?       我需要时间考虑
Now you press the button? I need time to think about it.
[08:57.90]你有12小时      是吗?
You have 12 hours. Have I?
[09:00.47]这只是你虚构的      您是今时的首相
You're inventing this. You are Prime Minister today.
[09:03.84]北约总部随时会来电话
The phone might ring now from NATO HQ.
[09:10.84]喂? 北约总部 首相
Hello...? Yes. NATO HQ, Prime Minister.
[09:16.66]您能参加四月的年会吗?
Can you address their annual conference in April?
[09:19.84]我以为可以的 现在我不大确定了
I thought I could. I'm not so sure now.
[09:22.51]是
Yes.
[09:24.47]第二步
Scenario two.
[09:26.63]俄国军队故意跨越了西德的国界
The Russian army cross the West German frontier.
[09:31.32]这是最后关头吗?      不是
Is that the last resort? No.
[09:33.88]好吧 第三步
Right, scenario three.
[09:36.20]假设俄国侵占了西德 比利时 荷兰 法国?
Suppose they invaded West Germany, Belgium, Holland, France?
[09:41.66]坦克到了英吉利海峡 整装待发了呢?
their troops have reached the Channel and are poised to invade?
[09:46.84]最后关头?      不
Is that the last resort? No.
[09:49.20]为什么?
Why not?
[09:50.88]我们参与核战的原因是保护自己
We'd only fight a nuclear war to defend ourselves.
[09:53.05]怎能用自杀保护自己?
That would be committing suicide!
[09:55.40]那什么才是最后关头 皮卡迪利(伦敦商业街)?
So what is the last resort? Piccadilly?
[09:59.39]沃特福峡谷维修站?
Watford Gap service station?
[10:02.08]革命剧院?
The Reform Club?
[10:04.35]也许核武防御根本没意义       它有
Maybe the nuclear deterrent makes no sense. Yes, it does.
[10:08.00]如果俄国或者美国有核弹 另一边必须也有
If the Russians or Americans have the bomb, so must the other
[10:12.15]留着北极星 以防万一      你的建议呢?
And keep Polaris just in case. What are you proposing?
[10:15.39]取消三叉戟订单 省下五十五亿 花在陆军上
Spend the ?5 billion you save on conventional forces.
[10:21.08]反正你又不会按那个按钮
You wouldn't really press the button.
[10:23.79]如果别无选择 我会的
I might if I had no choice.
[10:25.65]不会把你逼到别无选择 他们会用香肠战术
They'll never put you in a situation where you have no choice.
[10:30.90]假设我们取消三叉戟 把55亿花在陆军上
Supposing we cancel Trident and support conventional forces?
[10:36.08]我们要买什么 坦克?      不 要买ET
What do we spend it on? Tanks? No, we spend it on E.T.
[10:43.15]外星人?
Extra-terrestrials?
[10:45.78]紧急应对技术
Emergent technology.
[10:50.54]那是什么?      智能弹头
What's that? Smart missiles
[10:52.85]瞄准系统 红外线
target finding, infrared.
[10:54.75]谁来操纵ET呢?      一支庞大的陆军军队
Who would operate this E.T? A large conventional army.
[10:58.63]一支庞大的陆……
A large convention...
[11:00.78]我有个主意
I've got an idea.
[11:03.59]等等
Wait a minute!
[11:05.75]我觉得这个计划很可行 第一 取消三叉戟
I think I can see how to do this. First, we cancel Trident.
[11:09.66]对      也不再买巡航导弹了
Yes. We don't buy Cruise either.
[11:12.35]对      然后恢复征兵制
Yes. Then we introduce conscription.
[11:15.51]对
Yes.
[11:17.00]不仅解决了国防 还能解决就业问题
Not only solve defence problems but unemployment as well.
[11:22.08]首相 征兵会不会太有魄力?
Isn't conscription a courageous policy?
[11:24.78]魄力? 老天 会吗?
Courageous? Oh, my God, is it?
[11:28.63]不会不会 全额就业率的时候才会
No, no. In times of full employment, it would be.
[11:31.88]可现在我们只是
But now we'd just give
[11:33.17]给失业的年轻人找点事干
unemployed young people something to do.
[11:35.84]教他们各种技巧 甚至可能教会他们认字
teach them trades and skills. even teach them to read.
[11:40.00]文盲不能退伍 还能教他们讲点卫生
The army never discharged anyone who was illiterate.
[11:44.63]给年轻人全面教育 去弥补他们的素质教育
comprehensive education make up for comprehensive education
[11:51.88]就叫它"国民服务"把年轻人都送去社会服务
Call it national service. Send them into the community services
[11:57.03]同一个政策 可以解决
With one policy, we solve our
[11:59.23]国防 教育 就业问题 对吧教授?
defence, educational and unemployment problems.
[12:02.75]这真美妙 我可以预见
This is wonderful. I see it all now.
[12:05.71]"大不列颠的新未来 哈克的宏伟蓝图"
''A new deal for Britain Hacker's Grand Design.''
[12:10.42]有时 在我们伟大岛国
From time to time in our great island story,
[12:13.59]责任会降临于一人...
it falls to one man...
[12:16.63]领导人民走出阴影渊谷
to lead his people out of the valley of the shadow
[12:19.78]走向和平与繁荣之阳光高原
and into the sunlit uplands of peace and prosperity.
[12:25.51]为什么我以前就没想到呢?
Why didn't I think of this before?
[12:27.90]因为我们刚见面啊
Because we only just met.
[12:32.66]你好 亲爱的
Hello, darling!
[12:35.27]午餐吃什么?      你说呢
What's for lunch? You tell me.
[12:40.59]你要出去吗?      社工大会 我告诉过你了
Are you going somewhere? Voluntary services committee.
[12:44.75]噢 对 我想吃点炒蛋什么的
of course. I just thought a few scrambled eggs or something.
[12:49.71]我记得冰箱里还有些鸡蛋
I think there's some eggs in the fridge.
[12:52.35]我自己炒?      我们说好的 我继续工作
You want me to do it? We agreed that I'd carry on with my work.
